<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<worksheet xml:id="ws-right-triangle-trigonometry">
    <title>Right Triangle Trigonometry</title>
    <definition xml:id="def-six-trigonometric-functions-right-triangle">
        <statement>
            <p>
                Consider a right triangle whose short leg has length <m>a</m>, whose long leg has length <m>b</m>, and whose hypotenuse has length <m>c</m>. Let <m>\theta</m> be the angle opposite the short leg. 
            </p>
                <figure xml:id="fig-standard-right-triangle">
                    <caption>A right triangle where the short leg has length <m>a</m>, the long leg has length <m>b</m>, and the hypotenuse has length <m>c</m>. 
                        The vertex of the angle opposite to side <m>a</m> is labeled <m>A</m>, the vertex of the angle opposite to side <m>b</m> is labeled <m>B</m>, and the vertex of the right angle is labeled <m>C</m>. 
                        The angle <m>\angle CAB</m> is labeled <m>\theta</m>.</caption>
                    <image source="../../../assets/trigonometry/standard-right-triangle.png" width="50%" decorative="yes"/>
                </figure>
            <p>
                The six trigonometric functions of the angle <m>\theta</m> are defined as follows:
                <md>
                    <mrow> \sin(\theta)\amp=\frac{a}{c}=\frac{\text{opposite}}{\text{hypotenuse}}\amp\csc(\theta)\amp=\frac{c}{a}=\frac{\text{hypotenuse}}{\text{opposite}}</mrow>
                    <mrow> \cos(\theta)\amp=\frac{b}{c}=\frac{\text{adjacent}}{\text{hypotenuse}}\amp\sec(\theta)\amp=\frac{c}{b}=\frac{\text{hypotenuse}}{\text{adjacent}}</mrow>
                    <mrow> \tan(\theta)\amp=\frac{a}{b}=\frac{\text{opposite}}{\text{adjacent}}\amp\cot(\theta)\amp=\frac{b}{a}=\frac{\text{adjacent}}{\text{opposite}}</mrow>
                </md>                
            </p>
        </statement>
    </definition>
    <note>
        <p>
            The six trigonometric functions can be remembered using the mnemonic SOH-CAH-TOA, where
        </p>
    </note>
</worksheet>
